==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|nds-de|Snapps}}, originally “a sip (of liquor)”. Related to {{m|de|schnappen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ʃnaps/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schnaps.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Schnapses|Schnäpse|Schnäpschen}}

# [[spirit]], [[booze]], [[hard liquor]]

====Usage notes====
* Unlike {{cog|de|schnapps}}, the German word is general and does not refer to any specific kind of liquor. It is used, however, less commonly of more fancy or “sophisticated” kinds of spririts (such as whiskey).

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-m|es|pl=Schnäpse}}

